@startuml dvv-lost-write
title Algorithm 6.3 (corrected) — Figure 6 scenario: two clients, same server\nvectors ordered [A, B]

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam noteFontSize 11
skinparam ParticipantPadding 30

actor "Client 1" as C1
actor "Client 2" as C2
participant "Server A" as A
participant "Replica B" as B

note over A, B : Initially VV = [0,0], D = ∅ on both replicas

== Steps 1-2: both clients read ==
C1 -> A : GET
A --> C1 : x = 0, ctx {}
C2 -> A : GET
A --> C2 : x = 0, ctx {}
note over C1, A
  Algorithm 6.3 has no GET and no context input:
  what each client saw is never given to the server
end note

== Step 3: Client 1 writes ==
C1 -> A : PUT 10 (ctx {} is ignored)
activate A
note right of A #E8F5E9
  local: VV_A ← [1,0]
  d* = (A,1), D_A ← {(A,1)}
  ✓ no siblings existed, assumption holds
end note
A -> B : broadcast ([1,0], (A,1))
deactivate A
note right of B
  new? 1 ≤ VV_B[A]=0 → no, so new
  D_B = {(A,1)→10}, VV_B = [1,0]
end note

== Step 4: Client 2 writes ==
C2 -> A : PUT 20 (ctx {} is ignored)
activate A
note right of A #FFEBEE
  local: VV_A ← [2,0]
  d* = (A,2), D_A ← {(A,2)}
  ✗ Client 2 read before (A,1) existed,
     but 10 is discarded anyway
end note
A -> B : broadcast ([2,0], (A,2))
deactivate A
note right of B #FFEBEE
  new? 2 ≤ VV_B[A]=1 → no, so new
  prune (A,1): 1 ≤ VV_M[A]=2 ✓ → 10 removed
  D_B = {(A,2)→20}, VV_B = [2,0]
end note

note over A, B #FFEBEE
  Result: both replicas hold only {(A,2)→20}.
  Client 1's write is lost: VV_M = [2,0] claims
  the 20 write "saw" (A,1), but Client 2 never did.
end note

note over C1, B #E3F2FD
  With the client's context (paper's update(S, S_r, r), DVVS Put):
  Put(20, ctx=[0,0]) → is (A,1) known by ctx? 1 ≤ 0 → no, keep 10
  Result: {(A,1)→10, (A,2)→20}, two siblings, nothing lost
end note
@enduml
